  "body": "Part of #363 (research comment there has the sources and the safety reasoning).\n\nPriority: P1\n\nAdd op params:\n- infeed method: radial, modified flank with an angle, or alternating flank\n- first-pass depth\n- schedule: constant depth, or constant area by √n\n- minimum depth per pass\n- finish allowance\n- spring passes at full depth (default 0)\n\nThe kernel lays the passes from these. Flank infeed shifts each pass's station by depth·tan(angle) on the helix lattice, and the verdict reads the shifted V. `attach_cycle` fills the `ThreadCycle` fields from them.\n*Done means:* G32-pass output and the CL verdict follow each method and schedule. Pinning tests show the pass depths (√n with the Δdmin clamp), the flank station shift, and the spring-pass count for radial, flank and alternating infeed. The verdict stays clean on the modeled-thread fixture. A flank angle that does not fit the insert's included angle is refused at command creation. Changelog line.\n",
